Package: fsledger
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: INODE64 <ffelix@inode64.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: git (>= 1:2.36)
Recommends: ca-certificates, tzdata
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/inode64/fsledger
Description: file integrity monitoring with Git history and alerts
 fsledger detects unexpected file changes, records their contents in Git,
 keeps a catalog of hashes and metadata, and sends alerts and reports. When
 Linux provides the evidence, it also records the user and process that
 made each change.
 .
 The systemd unit is installed but neither enabled nor started: review the
 example configuration in /etc/fsledger first.
